{
  "staticFrameWarmsTheAccessList": {
    "_info": {
      "comment": "An INTERACTION: a STATICCALL cannot modify state, and the access list is NOT state for that purpose. An address first touched inside a read-only frame is warmed, and the warming SURVIVES the frame's return -- the next touch outside pays the warm price. Neither EIP-214's write protection nor EIP-2929's pricing says this on its own, and the natural reading of 'cannot modify state' gets it backwards.",
      "eips": "EIP-2929 at Magneto interacting with EIP-214 at Atlantis.",
      "theTwoReadings": {
        "0x30": "BALANCE on an address whose only prior touch was inside a STATICCALL. Must be WARM -- 107 from Magneto.",
        "0x31": "BALANCE on an address never touched. The control -- 2607."
      },
      "whatWriteProtectionACTUALLYForbids": "Read from the client's own guards rather than from the phrase: SSTORE, CREATE, CREATE2, a value-bearing CALL, SELFDESTRUCT, TSTORE and LOG each check the read-only flag themselves. The access list appears in none of them, and no gas function consults the flag. Warming is gas accounting, not a state mutation, and a read-only frame does it freely.",
      "theDefectThisCatches": "A client that implements write protection as a blanket ban on touching anything -- refusing to warm inside a static frame, or discarding the warming when the frame returns. Every later access to an address first seen inside a STATICCALL is then overcharged, and since read-only calls are how contracts inspect each other, that is a common path rather than an exotic one.",
      "measuredAgainstABrokenBuild": "A client patched to skip access-list warming while read-only is passed silently by ALL 41 other state fixtures in this suite and is caught here at 9/12 -- the three labels where cold and warm differ. That is the entire justification for the file and it was established before the file was kept.",
      "beforeMagnetoTheFileAssertsSAMENESS": "At Phoenix and earlier both slots read 707, because there is no cold/warm distinction. A client introducing access-list pricing too early fails those labels.",
      "oracle": "core-geth's own statetest runner, which is not the implementation under certification.",
      "oracle-version": "core-geth modernized 1.13.0-26975d6a. Production v1.12.21 cannot be used: its t8n fork table has no ETC_DieHard, ETC_Gotham or ETC_DefuseDifficultyBomb.",
      "wrongBuildScores": {
        "method": "Scored 2026-08-25 against a real broken build of the reference client, patched so gasEip2929AccountCheck does not add to the access list while the interpreter is read-only.",
        "correct": "12/12",
        "staticFrameDoesNotWarm": "9/12 here; 0 of the other 41 state fixtures catch it"
      },
      "generated": "2026-08-25",
      "signing": "txbytes carries the signed transaction. Legacy signature through Gas Reprice, replay-protected from Die Hard.",
      "unfilled-no-fork-name": "No expectation for ETC_Thanos: the generator's fork table has no name for it.",
      "unfilled-not-a-state-rule": "No expectation for ETC_DAOFork, ETC_DAOWars, ETC_FrontierThawing, ETC_MESSOff, ETC_MESSOn."
    },
